From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Widen license-files to cover vendored CPM dependencies

pyproject.toml declares the PEP 639 license-files = ["LICENSE"] as an
explicit list, so scikit-build-core's default LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/
NOTICE*/AUTHORS* glob never runs and only that one path is ever
collected. The wheel statically links several dependencies that
lib/cmake/scipp-cpm.cmake fetches and builds from source for every
wheel build (llnl/units, Boost headers, Eigen3) and dynamically links
oneTBB's built libtbb.so into the wheel itself (visible in the
published wheel as scipp/lib64/libtbb.so). None of those licences ship
in any published wheel; verified against the real scipp-26.8.0 wheels
on PyPI, which have the same gap.

Widening the explicit list to also match LICENSE.* lets the build add
LICENSE.units/LICENSE.boost/LICENSE.eigen/LICENSE.tbb at the project
root with no other packaging change (GoogleTest, the only other CPM
dependency, is test-only and never installed into the wheel).

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index eb38d37a6..b29e5cc93 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ name = "scipp"
 description = "Multi-dimensional data arrays with labeled dimensions"
 readme = "README.md"
 license = "BSD-3-Clause"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE", "LICENSE.*"]
 authors = [{ name = "Scipp contributors (https://github.com/scipp)" }]
 classifiers = [
   "Intended Audience :: Science/Research",
--
2.43.0
